hallenges. A No vote on a bill like that doesn't point to any one rung. The bill-text and bill-details pages belong to the same record.\n- **His Substack newsletter:** he says he offered an amendment to \"establish a non-partisan system of redistricting, in which no political data could be used\". These are his own words, coded `statement-other` and `direction-only`. They lean away from rung 5 (the majority party draws the maps) but never say who would draw them, so they can't separate rung 1 from rung 2 or the other rungs on that side.\n- **The caucus press release:** his quoted words call the new map cheating and rigging but name no policy, so I coded them `rhetorical`.\n- **`needs_source`:** the text of his HB 1032 amendment and the House roll call on it. If the amendment names who draws the maps (a citizens' commission or a commission with equal party seats), it could seat a chair.\n\nI coded both candidate quotes as not quotable: the newsletter line describes a past act (`not-forward`), and the press-release line is an attack (`is-attack`, `off-question`).","ttft_ms":22720,"type":"result","duration_ms":48387,"uuid":"9cab1669-ea00-4647-b1d8-758f675ea13b","ttft_stream_ms":1500,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":1500,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
